<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Reinforce with Leave-One-Out (RLOO) Baseline</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we describe here the implementation of RLOO that we
use, directly based on <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kool et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune with Reinforce using a per-prompt leave-one-out (LOO) group
baseline. At each update we draw a mini-batch of <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> distinct prompts
<math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{b}\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each prompt we sample <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> sequences
<math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{b,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b,g}</annotation></semantics></math> that contain a chain-of-thought (CoT) followed by a final
answer. Each such sequence provides a reward <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{b,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{b,g}</annotation></semantics></math> as described in
Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, the LOO group baseline for sample <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> averages the other <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\!-\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\!-\!1</annotation></semantics></math> rewards from the <em id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> prompt:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{r}_{b}^{(-g)}\;=\;\frac{1}{G-1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j=1\\
j\neq g\end{subarray}}^{G}r_{b,j},\qquad A_{b,g}\;=\;r_{b,g}-\bar{r}_{b}^{(-g)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{r}_{b}^{(-g)}\;=\;\frac{1}{G-1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j=1\\
j\neq g\end{subarray}}^{G}r_{b,j},\qquad A_{b,g}\;=\;r_{b,g}-\bar{r}_{b}^{(-g)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Baselines and rewards are treated as constants w.r.t. <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>; i.e., stop-gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{b,g,1:T_{b,g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b,g,1:T_{b,g}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote all tokens in <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{b,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b,g}</annotation></semantics></math> (CoT + answer). With policy <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the per-sequence log-probability is</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{b,g}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T_{b,g}}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{b,g,t}\mid y_{b,g,&lt;t},x_{b}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{b,g}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{T_{b,g}}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{b,g,t}\mid y_{b,g,&lt;t},x_{b}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Our loss is the advantage-weighted negative log-likelihood averaged over batch and group:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\;-\frac{1}{BG}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\sum_{g=1}^{G}A_{b,g}^{\mathrm{sg}}\,\ell_{b,g}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>sg</mi></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;-\frac{1}{BG}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\sum_{g=1}^{G}A_{b,g}^{\mathrm{sg}}\,\ell_{b,g},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\;-\frac{1}{BG}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\sum_{g=1}^{G}A_{b,g}\!\sum_{t=1}^{T_{b,g}}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{b,g,t}\mid y_{b,g,&lt;t},x_{b}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;-\frac{1}{BG}\sum_{b=1}^{B}\sum_{g=1}^{G}A_{b,g}\!\sum_{t=1}^{T_{b,g}}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{b,g,t}\mid y_{b,g,&lt;t},x_{b}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <sup id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A1.p4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sg</span></sup> denotes a stop-grad operator on the advantages.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Task Prompt</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To guide the model’s behavior during our experiments, we provided the following explicit instruction.
This prompt ensures that the assistant follows a structured reasoning process before giving the final answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="128.03" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 128.03" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,128.03) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#666666;" fill="#666666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 122.13 C 0 125.39 2.64 128.03 5.91 128.03 L 647.24 128.03 C 650.51 128.03 653.15 125.39 653.15 122.13 L 653.15 5.91 C 653.15 2.64 650.51 0 647.24 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 103.92 L 651.18 103.92 L 651.18 5.91 C 651.18 3.73 649.42 1.97 647.24 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 112.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="530.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:38.32em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Task Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 83.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.05em;font-size:10pt;" height="78.33" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.46)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A conversation between User and Assistant. The user asks a question, and the Assistant solves it.
The assistant first shows the complete reasoning process step by step, then provides the final answer in \boxed{}.
The assistant must always follow the format: ‘User: [question] Assistant: [detailed reasoning] The final answer is: \boxed{[answer]}.’
User: QUESTION Assistant: <span id="A2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Stopping Criterion and Prefilling</h2>

<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stopping Criterion.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hard:</span> Monitor the generated text and stop as soon as it ends with
<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The final answer is: </span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soft/Fuzzy:</span> During continuous generation, form a greedy shadow sequence by taking
the highest-probability hard token at each step and stop when this shadow ends with
<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The final answer is: </span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If neither condition is met, decoding continues until the maximum chain-of-thought
length <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prefilling.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If early stopping is reached, prefill <span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"> \boxed{</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is reached, prefill
<span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">The final answer is: \boxed{</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Hyperparameter Search</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models were trained with the AdamW optimizer and a cosine learning‐rate schedule using 20 warm up steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We tuned all hyperparameters using greedy validation performance. The learning rate and scale factors were used for fuzzy and soft, thus we only sweep over values for fuzzy.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning rate.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For both the hard and fuzzy, we swept over
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1\mathrm{e}{-5},\,9\mathrm{e}{-6},\,\dots,\,2\mathrm{e}{-6},\,1\mathrm{e}{-6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\mathrm{e}{-5},\,9\mathrm{e}{-6},\,\dots,\,2\mathrm{e}{-6},\,1\mathrm{e}{-6}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
for each combination of models.
The same optimal rates were found for both hard and fuzzy:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Llama 3B Instruct: <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Llama 8B Instruct: <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Qwen 3B Instruct: <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scale factor (Fuzzy only).</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We additionally swept scale factors
<math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.1,\dots,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.1,\dots,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> on the root mean square embedding norm
across various models and found <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.33</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.33</annotation></semantics></math> to be best, though most values below <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> performed well.
An ablation in Section <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Noise Scale ‣ Appendix F Ablations ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> supports the finding that our algorithm is robust to scale values below <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Results on Soft and Fuzzy Inference</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate base models and all RL trained models (hard, fuzzy and soft) under six inference settings: hard greedy, hard sample, fuzzy greedy, fuzzy sample, soft greedy and soft sample, described in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Here, we report test performance on GSM8K (Table <a href="#A5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix E Results on Soft and Fuzzy Inference ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), MATH-500 (Table <a href="#A5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix E Results on Soft and Fuzzy Inference ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and OlympiadBench (Table <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix E Results on Soft and Fuzzy Inference ‣ Soft Tokens, Hard Truths" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Contrary to previously reported benefits of soft inference on hard trained models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we do not observe any improvement in soft inference. Interestingly, we do not observe any gains of soft inference on soft trained models either. In our experiments, hard inference on all models achieves the best performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A5.T3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:155.1pt;vertical-align:-76.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-125.9pt,56.6pt) scale(0.57805733137163,0.57805733137163) ;">
